# Schema: Service-Owned + Pre-Upload Validation

RULE: Each service owns `schemas/output_schemas.py`. Call `validate_timestamp_date_alignment()` before every GCS write.
WHY: Schema drift causes silent data corruption downstream; misaligned timestamps cause partition read failures.
CODEX: 02-data/schema-governance.md

Service schema ownership:
  Each service repo owns: schemas/output_schemas.py
  Cross-cutting schemas (events, config): unified-trading-library owns them
  Never define output schemas in unified-trading-library for service-specific data

Pre-upload validation (required):
  from unified_domain_client import validate_timestamp_date_alignment
  validate_timestamp_date_alignment(df, date=processing_date)  # before every write

DO:
  # In your service
  from schemas.output_schemas import MyOutputSchema
  validate_timestamp_date_alignment(df, date=date)
  writer.write(df)  # only after validation passes

NEVER:
  Write to GCS without calling validate_timestamp_date_alignment first
  Define service-specific output schemas in unified-trading-library
  Share output schema definitions across services
